<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<widget xmlns:tizen="http://tizen.org/ns/widgets" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/widgets" id="https://tizenhomebrew.local" version="0.1.6" viewmodes="maximized">
    <access origin="*" subdomains="true"></access>
    <!-- The package id is arbitrary and is not a name: Tizen generates ten
         random characters and every tool here reads it back out of this file
         rather than hardcoding it.

         It has been changed once. A failed update left the previous id in a
         state the television would not install over — vd_appinstall answered
         every attempt with "Security error : Invalid function parameter was
         given:<2>", while the identical package under a different id installed
         at once, and nothing reachable through sdbd's command allowlist could
         clear it. If that ever happens again, changing this is the cure. -->
    <tizen:application id="GJBBYNLkgP.TizenHomebrew" package="GJBBYNLkgP" required_version="3.0"/>
    <author>Tizen Homebrew</author>
    <content src="ui/dist/tv.html"/>
    <feature name="http://tizen.org/feature/screen.size.all"/>
    <feature name="http://tizen.org/feature/web.service"/>
    <icon src="icon.png"/>
    <name>Tizen Homebrew</name>

    <!-- Every privilege here is public level, and that is a requirement rather
         than a coincidence: a partner-level privilege can only be carried by a
         partner-level distributor certificate, and a television refuses a
         package whose certificate does not reach far enough with

           install failed[118, -22], reason: Security error :
             :Invalid function parameter was given:<2>

         which names neither the privilege nor the certificate.

         Two Samsung privileges used to be declared here and are gone:
         network.public, because the service opens ordinary sockets from Node
         rather than calling webapis.network; and productinfo, because the
         platform version comes from tizen.systeminfo.getCapability, which is
         core Tizen and needs nothing. Neither was ever called. They cost every
         installation a partner certificate for capabilities this app does not
         use.

         A third has now joined them: packagemanager.info. Installed packages
         are read from /opt/usr/apps, one directory per package named by its
         id, because the API that privilege exists for — getPackagesInfo —
         blocks the service's thread for five minutes on Tizen 9. Nothing
         calls tizen.package any more, so nothing needs to ask for it.

         internet: reach the catalog origin and GitHub.
         application.launch: start the background service from the UI page. -->
    <tizen:privilege name="http://tizen.org/privilege/internet"/>
    <tizen:privilege name="http://tizen.org/privilege/tv.inputdevice"/>
    <tizen:privilege name="http://tizen.org/privilege/application.launch"/>
    <tizen:privilege name="http://tizen.org/privilege/unlimitedstorage"/>

    <tizen:profile name="tv-samsung"/>

    <!-- The headless half: serves the phone UI and drives SDB over loopback.
         The id suffix must match what tv.html launches. -->
    <tizen:service id="GJBBYNLkgP.TizenHomebrewService">
        <tizen:content src="service/dist/index.js"/>
        <tizen:name>TizenHomebrewService</tizen:name>
        <tizen:description>Serves the Tizen Homebrew UI and installs packages over loopback SDB.</tizen:description>
    </tizen:service>

    <!-- background-support is "disable" so Back actually ends the page. Enabled,
         the runtime keeps it alive in the background and the theme audio plays on
         over the Tizen home screen. The service above is a separate application
         and keeps running either way. -->
    <tizen:setting screen-orientation="landscape" context-menu="disable" background-support="disable" encryption="disable" install-location="auto" hwkey-event="enable"/>
</widget>
